before:
```typescript
interface Card { id: number; title: string; note: string }
type CardText = Pick<Card, "title" | "note">;
```
CardText describes title and note, not id. It does not remove fields from an existing runtime object.

```typescript
type TextPatch = Partial<{title: string; note: string}>;
const patch: TextPatch = {note: "Updated"};
```
Leaving title out means this patch supplies no new title.

after:
This update type allows only title and note, and either can be omitted.
```typescript
interface Card { id: number; title: string; note: string; }
type TextPatch = Partial<Pick<Card, "title" | "note">>;
const patch: TextPatch = { note: "Updated" };
```
The ID is not an editable field in this type.
